{"title":"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When three consecutive positive integers are multiplied together, the answer is always\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12c1f5c39d718f2cc362c4822ee03f302a4cf9bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\text{odd} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\text{a multiple of } 6 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\text{a multiple of } 12 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\text{a multiple of } 4 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\text{a multiple of } 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"806\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest number of the three consecutive numbers. Since the numbers are consecutive, the other two numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6bcde0e66de78dde6250138abf955e45c4ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a186a5fd4879b180d5d4f42ddeb6bec9af98478b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Using this, the product of the numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3efc306cb42b61c2edbf033ce593c02fe9fc96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x + 1)(x + 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is even, the whole product must be even because an even number multiplied by another integer must also be even. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6bcde0e66de78dde6250138abf955e45c4ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> must be even because an odd number added to an odd number is even, so the whole product must be even for the same reason. This means that this product must be even no matter what.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150b9283a4dc35e62a4c1bb470b9cf4f70eefbe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x + 1)(x + 2) = x(x^2 + 3x + 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then this whole product must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is one of the factors. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then it still must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f30a26245fcbb2fdee44e17b7c11e3603324b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{2} + 3 \\times 1 + 2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then it still must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/5281ab62163455259ef6610e2b5f85e0ba7566c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2} + 3 \\times 2 + 2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since the value of the product is even and is also divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0601bc67b20c9d72794553223bf22905f6a570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\text{a multiple of } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"155\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Specific_Numbers.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Specific_Numbers)\">Solution 2 (Specific Numbers)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Specific Numbers)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are consecutive positive integers, so we can use them for this problem.\n</p><p>The product of these numbers would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee172349925189a9f5e614a3e7e0660176a12da1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 2 \\times 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Of the answer choices, the only one that matches is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0601bc67b20c9d72794553223bf22905f6a570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\text{a multiple of } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"155\" height=\"30\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is an even number, so it is <i>not</i> odd. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as it is equal to itself. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d251ecee7e7e6a5f99f11326bc747c376cd5cd11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 &lt; 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is also <i>not</i> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley\">2009 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 22 (page does not exist)\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 23 (page does not exist)\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"CEMC Cayley\">CEMC Cayley</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221538\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 284/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2050/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 310/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion 